    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d111">

                <pb facs="0170" n="162" xml:id="pg162"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/7468: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Then in France, to the Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">St.
                                Jean de Luz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-03-08T13:00:00+00:00">March 8, 1938—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 9—11:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>459. Defeat in first naval battle and loss of the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Baleares</hi>, the flag and star ship of insurgents, severe blow to
                    Franco’s prestige, and rebel papers thus far have suppressed the slightest
                    references to it. Prieto’s claim to have created a new navy as well as army not
                    improbable. Government now has advantage in ships and if crews and officers are
                    now trained effect on the war far reaching.</p>
                <p>2. Understood here that 5,000 more troops from Libya just landed at Cadiz, half
                    from Italian hospital ship <hi rendition="#italic">Gradisca</hi>, half from
                    warships including destroyer flotilla. These said to have been sent to
                    Guadalajara front. Bay may be able to verify since troops would have gone
                    through Seville.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
